{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd","id":1401296,"title":"Where is the moving of the Imperial Manse discused? (1st & 2nd)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-06T01:40:55-07:00","id":1401296,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Where is the moving of the Imperial Manse discused? (1st & 2nd)","content":"I remember the Imperial Manse was moved from the top of the Imperial Mountain, but I can't recall which book discuses the why &amp; such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:58:33-07:00","id":1401302,"title":"","content":"Moved?<br /> <br /> IIRC: The Sword exists inside the Imperial Mountain. The control room has always been where it is (where the Empress built the Imperial City). There used to be a targeting array satellite above Mount Meru.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for something contradictory, I think you're best served looking for books about Autochothon, because they might mention something of its construction.<br /> <br /> Lands of Creation has this to say:<br /> <br /> All but the oldest and most powerful Exalts imagine that the Sword, in its entirety, is located in the powerful manse called the Orichalcum Shrine at the mouth of the Dawn River. The shrine, a narrow spire of adamant hundreds of feet high and delicately webbed with orichalcum, was built using the same techniques designed for the war manses and the Last Supplicant of Endless Power (see p. 93). It is equipped with limited self-guided defense mechanisms and a dozen or more powerful spirits bound to its service, and it\u2019s keyed to only a handful of Exalted. It is certainly impressive enough\u2014to the ignorant\u2014but the Orichalcum Shrine is only the focusing mechanism, where Essence and will merge to create the most destructive forces seen in Creation since the Primordials themselves. The actual Sword itself is located at the center of the Blessed Isle, within Mount Meru. It stretches from beneath the Holy Peak, thousands of feet straight down through the mountain, and farther still\u2014as far as any Exalt or god can explore. It pierces the very heart of Creation, and Essence throbs and thunders in it like a gigantic heartbeat.<br /> <br /> At first glance, the Sword of Creation is simply impossible. It is a massive seam of all the natural magical materials merged into a huge, twisted column stabbed through the Blessed Mountain. The Essence contained within it is so powerful that the very air around it is deadly to the careless. Rock around the Sword is full of peculiar inclusions, unusually large deposits of naturally occurring magical materials, various crystals that share many properties with hearthstones, and occasionally peculiar living organisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T04:08:32-07:00","id":1401312,"title":"","content":"The only reference to the idea of the Imperial Manse being moved that I can recall is a scenario in Return of the Scarlet Empress where Neighbourhood Relocation Technique is employed on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T07:02:49-07:00","id":1401335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401312#post1401312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reference to the idea of the Imperial Manse being moved that I can recall is a scenario in Return of the Scarlet Empress where Neighbourhood Relocation Technique is employed on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This bit was in the <i>Under the Rose</i> adventure, in which the players explore the underbelly of the Imperial Manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T04:42:30-07:00","id":1401658,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe it was a group hallucination, but I also remember something somewhere mentioning that the control room for the Sword was originally at the top of Meru, snd was moved to its current location early in the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:10:10-07:00","id":1401745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401658#post1401658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, maybe it was a group hallucination, but I also remember something somewhere mentioning that the control room for the Sword was originally at the top of Meru, snd was moved to its current location early in the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that's Under the Rose, it's information the quest giver drops in. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Heron, Under the Rose page 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My last incarnation helped drag the manse down the mountain to Vanchow during the Aftershock War, so I like to think I know a thing or two about it. Now that was a Neighborhood Relocation Scheme!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:51:29-07:00","id":1401753,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m almost certain that the First Age capital of Meru is located at the top of the Imperial Mountain, while the Imperial City built during the Shogunate period and later ruled by the Scarlet Empress is located at the base of the mountain. Not sure about the other stuff.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> am I right about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:03:02-07:00","id":1401757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401753#post1401753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m almost certain that the First Age capital of Meru is located at the top of the Imperial Mountain, while the Imperial City built during the Shogunate period and later ruled by the Scarlet Empress is located at the base of the mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid that's not correct - the Imperial City is not at the base of the mountain, it's far to the east, on the east coast of the Blessed Isle. See <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/JD36YlI.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this map</a> for the 3e version, but that's been the position of the Imperial City since at least 2nd Edition, and I believe 1st Edition as well.<br /> <br /> Also, the Imperial City wasn't built in the Shogunate (at least for both 3e and 2e). It wasn't built until after the Great Contagion/Crusade, when the Empress made it her capital, since it was the location of the Imperial Manse, which nobody could access or use during the Shogunate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:53:51-07:00","id":1401776,"title":"","content":"Okay. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:12:02-07:00","id":1401783,"title":"","content":"And you\u2019re right. I think Lookshy was the capital of the Shogunate, except it had a different name back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:27:08-07:00","id":1401784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401783#post1401783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lookshy was the capital of the Shogunate, except it had a different name back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to pick on you here! But I don't think that's correct either, either in 2e or 3e. Lookshy (called Deheleshen at that time) might have been <i>a</i> capital of the Shogunate at one point, but I don't think it was ever stated to be, and even if it was, it wouldn't likely have been the capital for the whole of the Shogunate's history. Remember, the Shogunate was a time of significant civil war, where many Dragon-Blooded commanders attempted to claim the title for themselves. If they had a set capital (not all states do), I'd think it would move around as the ruler changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T23:05:40-07:00","id":1401858,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s okay \ud83d\ude0a. And yeah, that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T04:58:08-07:00","id":1401894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401757#post1401757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's far to the east, on the east coast of the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>More inland and upriver than coastal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T05:15:19-07:00","id":1402226,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Shogunate capital of the Blessed Isle was Lords Crossing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T09:32:28-07:00","id":1402263,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> thank you \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, is Heirs to the Shogunate coming out on DTRPG soon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T10:42:58-07:00","id":1402269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1401783#post1401783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you\u2019re right. I think Lookshy was the capital of the Shogunate, except it had a different name back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy was built off the corpse of the city Deheleshan, it wasn't the capital though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T16:49:51-07:00","id":1402331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401296-where-is-the-moving-of-the-imperial-manse-discused-1st-2nd?p=1402263#post1402263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, is Heirs to the Shogunate coming out on DTRPG soon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not for a while. I'd guess at least a year. The Heirs manuscript was released to backers of the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter a couple months ago, but that was just the manuscript. As I understand it, the manuscript for Heirs was roughly in the same point in the process that the manuscript for What Fire Hath Wrought was at when the actual DB Kickstarter campaign was running, and that took over a year from the Kickstarter campaign to What Fire Hath Wrought being released on DriveThruRPG. Heirs is shorter than WFHW, of course, but I wouldn't expect a significantly shorter process for it, so don't hold your breath. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T18:58:26-07:00","id":1402345,"title":"","content":"Thank you \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}